  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$",
